---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { ASK_SERVER, CONTACT_EMAIL, COZMC } from '../config';
---
<Prose title="Privacy" description="What NerdyBirdie LLC Gaming Guides stores and what it doesn't.">
  <p class="muted">Last updated 24 November 2026. NerdyBirdie LLC Gaming Guides is run by NerdyBirdie LLC.</p>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>No accounts, no analytics, no ads, no tracking cookies. Your progress and settings stay in your browser.{!ASK_SERVER && ' ASK "COZMC" runs on your device and doesn\'t send your questions anywhere.'}</p>
  <h2>What's stored on your device</h2>
  <p>Ticks, saved items, notes, your spoiler and platform settings, and where you left off are kept in your browser's local storage on this
  device. They aren't sent to us. Clearing your browser's site data deletes them, so use <a href="/progress/">My progress</a> to download a backup.</p>
  <p>To continue in another browser, My progress can make a <strong>transfer link</strong>. Your progress is packed into the part of the link after "#",
  which browsers don't send to any server, so it doesn't pass through us. Anyone you give the link to can load that progress, so share it only with yourself.</p>
  <h2>ASK "COZMC"</h2>
  {ASK_SERVER
    ? <p>When you ask a question, it's sent to our server to search the guide. Questions the guide can't answer are kept (without your IP address) so we can improve the guide. Don't include personal details in questions.</p>
    : <p>ASK "COZMC" searches our published guide inside your browser. Your questions aren't sent to us or to any AI service, and aren't stored.</p>}
  <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
  <p>We don't run analytics or advertising scripts, and fonts are served from this site. If we ever add privacy-friendly usage statistics, accounts or an online assistant, this page will say so first.</p>
  <h2>Videos and outside links</h2>
  <p>Creator videos (YouTube, Twitch or TikTok) only load after you press play. At that point that service receives your request under its own privacy policy.
  Links to Discord, cozmc.us, Rockstar Games and other sites open those sites, which have their own policies.</p>
  <h2>What's New from creators (YouTube API Services)</h2>
  <p>Our server checks a short list of approved creators' public YouTube uploads once a day using the YouTube API Services.
  It keeps only each video's id, title, channel name and upload date, for at most 7 days unless it's checked again, and
  never any information about you. Your browser asks only our site for this list; nothing is sent to YouTube until you open a video.
  By using this feature you agree to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>;
  Google's handling of data is covered by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>Our host (Netlify) processes basic request logs, such as IP addresses, to deliver and protect the site.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{CONTACT_EMAIL ? <>Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</> : <>Ask in the <a href={COZMC.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener">COZMC Discord</a>. A contact email will be added before public launch.</>}</p>
</Prose>
